  partName: Cap2
  description: The Cap3 is a tiny, elongated component situated at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, fabricated from Shaft1 material, functioning as a protective
    covering for the engine's shaft. Its primary purpose is to safeguard the shaft
    from damage and ensure the engine's overall integrity, thereby maintaining reliability
    and performance. Notably, the Cap3 is carefully balanced to minimize vibration
    and noise during engine operation, contributing to a smoother and more efficient
    flight experience.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
